From: Balena RK3588 integration
Subject: [PATCH] setexpr: store arithmetic results as decimal

meta-balena's rollback environment (env_resin.h) drives hostapp A/B
rollback entirely through u-boot env scripting:

  setexpr bootcount ${bootcount} + 1
  ...
  if test ${bootcount} -gt ${os_bc_lim}; then    /* roll back  */
  if test ${resin_root_part} = ${resin_roota}; then  /* pick slot */

This tree stores setexpr results with env_set_hex(), i.e. "0x"-prefixed
hex strings, while cmd/test.c parses numeric operands with
simple_strtol(arg, NULL, 10).  strtol("0x4", 10) stops at 'x' and
yields 0, so the bootcount limit comparison isalways false and the slot
comparison compares "4" against "0x4" as strings.  Both rollback
decisions in resin_check_altroot can never trigger on this u-boot
(E1 board experiment: bootcount.env updated to "bootcount=0x2" each
boot while no partition flip ever happened with bootcount preseeded
past the limit).

The default environment on this device uses setexpr arithmetic only
inside env_resin.h (bootcount, resin_roota, resin_rootb); nothing else
consumes its output format.  Store the operator result with
env_set_ulong() so the value round-trips as plain decimal through
os_inc_bc_save's "env export/fatwrite bootcount.env" and matches both
the decimal test comparisons and the decimal resin_root_part written
by the OS-side 99-resin-uboot hook.

---
--- a/cmd/setexpr.c
+++ b/cmd/setexpr.c
@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@
 		return 1;
 	}
 
-	env_set_hex(argv[1], value);
+	env_set_ulong(argv[1], value);
 
 	return 0;
 }
